skills.card:
averageWordLength — Work out the typical word size in a text — its average word length.
  needs: text: string
  e.g. "average word length of this sentence" → {"text":"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog"}

convertCase — Change text to another capitalisation — title case, upper, lower, camelCase, snake_case.
  needs: text: string, style: string
  e.g. "make this title case: the lord of the rings" → {"text":"the lord of the rings","style":"title"}

countCharacters — Count the characters in a text — with spaces, without spaces, and how many are letters or digits.
  needs: text: string
  e.g. "how many characters is this" → {"text":"The quick brown fox."}

countLines — Count the lines in a block of text, separating blank lines from lines with content.
  needs: text: string
  e.g. "how many lines is this" → {"text":"one\ntwo\nthree"}

countSentences — Count the sentences in a text, and the average sentence length.
  needs: text: string
  e.g. "how many sentences is this" → {"text":"Hello there. How are you today? I am well."}

countWords — Measure how long a piece of text is: its total words, characters, sentences and paragraphs.
  needs: text: string
  e.g. "how many words is this paragraph" → {"text":"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog."}

detectLanguage — Guess which language a piece of text is written in.
  needs: text: string
  e.g. "what language is this" → {"text":"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog and then it goes to sleep"}

extractCurrencyAmounts — Pull every money amount out of a text, with its currency.
  needs: text: string
  e.g. "get the amounts from this invoice line" → {"text":"subtotal £120.50, shipping £4.99"}

extractNumbers — Take the plain figures out of a text, thousands separators and decimals handled.
  needs: text: string
  e.g. "get the numbers from: we sold 1,250 units at £3.99 each" → {"text":"we sold 1,250 units at £3.99 each"}

extractTimes — Pull every clock time out of a text and give each in 24-hour form.
  needs: text: string
  e.g. "get the times from this message" → {"text":"the meeting is 9:30am and lunch at 1pm"}

flagProfanity — Flag swear words in text against a word list.
  needs: text: string
  e.g. "check this for swearing" → {"text":"What a bloody mess this is"}

